+
+# Message Count Sorting
+
+- The resume picker's Sort controls cycle through Updated, Created and Messages.
+- Message counts are requested and computed only after selecting Messages.
+- Counts include user messages and every assistant message phase, including commentary, partial answers, final answers and older messages without a phase.
+- Reasoning, tool activity and other non-message items are excluded.
+- Messages replaces the existing time field in comfortable and dense views.
+- Title rendering remains unchanged.
+- Message counts add no column.
+- Expanded session details also show the count while Messages is selected.
+- Pending counts display 0.
+- Failed reads display Error.
+- The picker reports the server's count-read error.
+- Read failures do not become successful zero counts.
+- The existing asynchronous listing continues across all eligible pages.
+- Older sessions participate in count sorting.
+- Single-word titles remain pinned.
+- Count ties use descending creation time.
+- Existing directory, provider, status and search filters still apply.
+- Count requests and calculation leave navigation and other picker operations available.
+- Changing the sort cancels queued count work.
+- Reloading the listing cancels queued count work.
+- Closing the picker cancels queued count work.
+- Stale results do not change the current listing.
+- An already admitted native read may finish after cancellation.
+- Counts remain in the current picker listing only.
+- A new Messages listing reads counts again.
+- Message counting adds no standing index.
+- Message counting adds no disk cache.
+- Default thread listing remains unchanged.
+- Time sorting remains unchanged.
+- The fork picker retains its original two sort choices.
